en:
I see.
You're quite the romantic, aren't you?
Then if I asked you to make me your sweetheart, would you do it?{p}

Don't forget what you just said.
You must never, ever forget it.
Because the story I'm about to tell you is about two people who were in love.{p}

Date had to stay late for club activities.
Even if he went home now and called, he wouldn't make it in time.
So he called from school.{p}

Yaguchi thought to herself.
She wasn't the one at fault.
Date was the one who was wrong.{p}

But to Yaguchi, that didn't matter.
All she wanted was for the usual gentle Date to come back.
And she decided that tonight, for sure, the two of them would talk on the phone.{p}

She lost count of how many times she called after that.
Even so, the line stayed busy the whole time.
Then a thought suddenly struck Yaguchi.{p}

I have to hurry.
That's what she thought, and she got ready at once.
But halfway through taking off her pajamas and changing her clothes, a thought struck her.{p}

She slipped quietly out of the house and hurried to the school.
She went as fast as she could, but there was no one to be seen at the back gate.
When she looked at her watch, it was already past eleven.{p}

The cord stretched out and wound itself around and around her neck.
She was choking, and when she opened her mouth wide to scream, the receiver suddenly leapt into it.
All the while spewing out that thick, cloudy white liquid.{p}

So without the slightest hesitation, he let her into his house.
Inside the house, too, her manner didn't change.
She acted as if she'd come over many times and knew the place well.{p}

She turned to face Higashiyama.
"Too bad... it very nearly worked.
I blew it."{p}

Her hand was chilly, cold as ice.
"☆"
I caught my breath before I could stop myself.{p}

The two of them went to a park in the neighborhood.
It was dusk, you see, and the swings and the slide were all dyed crimson.
There, the girl turned around to face Higashiyama.{p}

"Thank you... I'm so happy.
Don't you ever forget me again."
Then she turned her back and ran off.{p}

...I see. What a shame.
Oh yes, it was the seven wonders, wasn't it?
It's a short story, but do you mind?{p}

In that instant, the charm turned into a powerful curse and struck her instead.
They say the headache was two or three times worse than the boy's suffering.
And as a result, she died.{p}

But even so, she was content.
After all, she had protected the one she loved.
Surely he would remember her, too... I imagine that's what she thought.{p}

You don't dislike them...
Does that mean you like them?
Am I wrong?{p}

I'm not wrong, am I?
...That's good.
For me, and for you too.{p}

...You know, right now you're very much on my mind.
{a}.
What would you do if I asked you to make me your lover?{p}

How cruel...
Making a girl confess to you and then saying that - don't you think that's going too far?
In that case, I won't tell any scary story.{p}

"...Be my lover."
No way!
That's blackmail!{p}

"I'm so glad!
Then I'll tell it."
Iwashita smiled sweetly and went on with her story.{p}

In that case, maybe the letters were stuck to the back of the mailbox or somewhere.
It'd be terrible if someone else saw them, wouldn't it?
So after school, the two of them decided to go to that mailbox and look.{p}

Worse still, the mailbox began swallowing her arm instead.
It swallowed more and more of her, until in the end her whole body had slipped right inside the mailbox.
And so, Yaguchi vanished.{p}

And that's the end of my story.
But the power of love is amazing, isn't it?
It can give that kind of power even to an inanimate object.{p}

...I see. What a shame.
And I really did like you, {a}.
It's sad, but it can't be helped.{p}

The next moment, a scream rang out.
It was Date.
"Agh, it hurts! Let go of me☆"{p}

She picked up the receiver at once.
Date had called her after all.
The moment she thought that, she forgot all about the resolve she'd had just a moment ago.{p}

"I'm sorry.
It's because I didn't explain properly..."
She started to say that without even checking who it was.{p}

Yes, that's a good idea.
Whoever is interfering knows the two of them call each other at nine p.m.
So if they change the time, it's sure to work.{p}

There was nothing there but a phone booth, standing all alone under a dim streetlight as if someone had left it behind and forgotten it.
Yaguchi waited there for a while.
But Date's parents didn't come.{p}

She couldn't wait to get to school.
She practically ran the whole way.
Because she wanted to see Date as soon as she possibly could.{p}

Apparently, a dog's carcass had been stuffed inside the pay phone booth by the back gate.
And it was a gruesome one, burned raw by some chemical or something, I hear.
From that day on, the fake calls to Yaguchi's house stopped.{p}

How do I know all this, you ask?
Heh heh heh... I wonder.
What does it matter?{p}

Yaguchi couldn't make up her mind.
So she decided to wait and see for a while.
The phone kept on ringing.{p}

That's right, she hung up the phone.
But she shouldn't have done that.
Because it made something terrible happen.{p}

There was a sickening thunk.
The sound of Iwashita's head hitting the corner of a desk.
I rushed over to her where she had fallen.{p}

"You humiliated me... I won't forgive you.
I'm going to put a curse on you...!"
A violent wave of dizziness hit me.{p}

Iwashita smirked.
"You've got less backbone than I thought.
You're someone I actually fell for, so I wanted you to hold out a little longer."{p}

"Did you think you could escape?
It's no use... I will never, ever let you go."
A violent wave of dizziness hit me.{p}
